From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nate Chapin <japhet@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 13:39:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 07/14] [WebApp] Require committed nav for WebAppUrlLoader
 DidFinishLoad

`WebAppUrlLoader::LoaderTask::DidFinishLoad` previously classified a
load as `kUrlLoaded` solely by comparing the renderer-supplied
`validated_url` from `blink.mojom.LocalFrameHost.DidFinishLoad` against
`url_`, without verifying that a cross-document navigation for the
current `LoaderTask` ever committed or that the frame's committed URL
still matched `url_`. In a shared background `WebContents`
(`WebContentsManager::shared_web_contents_`), a renderer could stall
pending navigations (`PrepareForLoad(about:blank)` and `LoadUrl(url)`)
and send spoofed `DidFinishLoad` IPCs while its own document remained
committed, causing `ExternalAppResolutionCommand` to read manifest data
from the wrong origin.

This CL hardens `WebAppUrlLoader` and `ExternalAppResolutionCommand`:
1. Tag `WebAppUrlLoaderNavigationHandleData` with a
   `base::WeakPtr<const LoaderTask>` (`IsForLoaderTask(this)`) and track
   `has_committed_navigation_` in `LoaderTask::DidFinishNavigation`
   (only set on primary main-frame, cross-document commits matching
   `url_` under `url_comparison_`).
2. If a cross-document target navigation (`!url_.IsAboutBlank()`) aborts
   without committing (`!navigation_handle->HasCommitted()`) before any
   commit for the task, fail immediately with `kFailedUnknownReason`
   rather than stalling the command queue until the 30s load timeout
   (note: non-committing responses such as 204/205/downloads now report
   `kFailedUnknownReason` / `kInstallURLLoadFailed` instead of timing
   out with `kFailedPageTookTooLong` / `kInstallURLLoadTimeOut`).
3. Reorder `LoaderTask::OnLoadUrlTimeout` to call
   `PostResultTask(kFailedPageTookTooLong)` (which calls
   `Observe(nullptr)`) before `contents->Stop()`, because `Stop()`
   synchronously aborts the pending navigation and would otherwise
   re-enter `DidFinishNavigation` and consume `callback_` twice.
4. Gate `LoaderTask::DidFinishLoad` and `DidFailLoad` on
   `has_committed_navigation_`, check `render_frame_host->IsErrorDocument()`,
   verify `render_frame_host->GetLastCommittedURL()` matches `url_`
   under `url_comparison_` (returning `kRedirectedUrlLoaded` if the
   document changed its URL after commit), and require
   `validated_url == last_committed_url` before reporting `kUrlLoaded`.
5. Add a defense-in-depth check in
   `ExternalAppResolutionCommand::ContinueUpdateInfoWithParamsAndUpgradeLock`
   verifying that `web_app_info_->manifest_id().value()` remains
   same-origin with `install_options_.install_url`, routing mismatches
   through `OnUrlLoadedAndBranchInstallation(kRedirectedUrlLoaded)` so
   placeholder fallback is preserved when `install_placeholder` is set.

Fixed: 562230299, 497098609
Test: components_unittests --gtest_filter="WebAppUrlLoaderTest.*"
Test: unit_tests --gtest_filter="ExternalAppResolutionCommandTest.*"
Test: browser_tests --gtest_filter="ExternallyManagedAppManagerBrowserTest.*"
